      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Microwave promoted high yielding synthesis of 4-aminoquinoline-phthalimides was developed with an aim to evaluate their anti-plasmodial potential. The scaffolds with longer spacer length (n = 6, 8) between two pharmacophores and a halogen substituent on the phthalimide ring displayed good antiplasmodial activity. Compound 5w, with an optimum combination of hexyl chain as spacer along with a tetra-bromophthalimide ring proved to be most potent and non-cytotoxic among the series exhibiting an IC50 value of 0.10 μM."
      },
